summary:
  A property or a function that its object does not have passes the lint,
  as it did while the pass looked only for a handful of words.

history:
  The old pass failed on a nonzero exit and on messages that said
  duplicate, syntax, unavailable or error. "Member … not found on type …"
  says none of them: root.eiOleOlemasKanaar() in main.qml was found by
  qmllint and the lint stayed green. Since 2026-11-12 every message fails
  the lint unless it is an unqualified access or a var in a block, the two
  kinds healthy code produces by the hundred, or a counted row accounts
  for it; a config key is looked up in main.xml instead.

target:
  scripts/qmllint_gate.py

find:
          if category == "unqualified" and message == "Unqualified access":

replace:
          if category in ("unqualified", "missing-property"):

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_qmllint_gate.py::test_a_member_that_does_not_exist_is_reported_though_a_loop_follows
  on a real qmllint, and by tests/test_qmllint_gate.py::test_the_verdict_on_one_file
  and tests/test_qmllint_gate.py::test_a_config_key_is_checked_against_main_xml
  on reports made by hand.
